<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Inhambane</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Inhambane is a port town on a sheltered bay on the coast of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mozambique">Mozambique</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vasco-da-gama">Vasco da Gama</a> called there in 1498, and Portuguese traders were active in the 16th century, dealing in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> and later in slaves. In the 19th century its hinterland was contested with the Gaza kingdom, and the town is now the capital of Inhambane Province.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/inhambane.jpg" alt="Inhambane" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Oscar Wagenmans · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Esta%C3%A7%C3%A3o_do_Caminho_de_Ferro_Inhambane_back_side.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
